# Force LF line endings on checkout for EVERY text file. Git on Windows
# defaults to autocrlf=true and converts LF→CRLF on checkout, which
# corrupts shebangs (`#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n`) and breaks regex
# literals containing CJK characters when the parser is confused by
# carriage returns. Symptoms on Windows CI:
#   - tests/hooks/user-prompt-intent.test.ts collection fails with
#     "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" because the JS file
#     was checked out with CRLF endings.
#   - All hooks scripts (which start with #!/usr/bin/env node) become
#     unrunnable when invoked directly.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` rather than a list of extensions.
#
# The list version covered the ten extensions whose breakage had been
# noticed, and left `.css`, `.html`, `.svg`, `.py`, `.toml`, `.map`,
# `LICENSE`, `CODEOWNERS` and every future extension uncovered. That is
# how the Windows CI legs failed on this branch: `dashboard/index.html`
# and `dashboard/src/styles/global.css` were checked out with CRLF, vite
# INLINED them into `dashboard/dist/index.html`, and the carriage returns
# landed mid-line inside the bundle — a real content difference that
# line-ending normalisation cannot undo, so the committed artifact could
# never be reproduced on Windows. Line endings are a property of text,
# not of a list of suffixes somebody remembered to extend.
#
# Binaries below are exempted explicitly; `text=auto` also leaves any file
# Git detects as binary alone, so an unlisted binary format is safe by
# default rather than corrupted by default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — never auto-modify.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.node binary
